Here is a simple example of how that looks in code:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");

    // Option 1: Natural termination (most common)
    // The program ends here when main() finishes.

    // Option 2: Explicit termination
    // exit(0); // 0 indicates a successful exit

    return 0;
}
```

